("1. Three bowls out on the grass, well apart, filled from the tap with the jugs. She carries them out one at a time.\n2. Colour each bowl a different colour, one bottle per bowl, and she does the squeezing.\n3. Give her the cups and let her pour red into blue for as long as it takes the whole bowlful to turn.\n4. Funnel into a cup next, then funnel into a bowl, then funnel held over her own foot.\n5. Hand her the sieve and say nothing about it. She will try to carry water in it three or four times before she gives up on it.\n6. Kreston's shallow tray goes on a towel at the far end, two centimetres of clear water, and it is his alone.\n7. Tip every bowl out onto the grass before anyone goes inside, and bring the towels in with you.",
 "1. Three bowls out on the grass, well apart, filled from the tap with the jugs. She carries them out one at a time.\n2. Colour each bowl differently, one bottle per bowl, and she does the squeezing.\n3. Give her the cups and let her pour red into blue for as long as it takes the whole bowlful to turn.\n4. Funnel into a cup next, then funnel into a bowl, then funnel over her own foot.\n5. Hand her the sieve and say nothing about it. She will try to carry water in it three or four times.\n6. Kreston's shallow tray goes on a towel at the far end, two centimetres of clear water, his alone.\n7. Tip every bowl out onto the grass before anyone goes in, and bring the towels with you."),
