("1. Spread the torn paper across the tray and hold a balloon a hand's width above it. Nothing moves, and she needs to see that first.\n2. Rub the same balloon on her hair, twenty strokes, counted out by her.\n3. Hold it back over the tray at the same height. The paper comes up off the metal to meet it.\n4. Rub a second balloon on the wool jumper and run the same test. Ask her to call which one lifted more before either of you looks.\n5. Go hunting with it. Balloon behind her head and her hair follows it. Balloon beside a thin stream from the kitchen tap and the water bends over. Balloon near the crisp packet on the floor and the packet slides.\n6. Let her find one more thing in the house that moves. She will try twenty and land one.",
 "1. Spread the torn paper across the tray and hold a balloon a hand's width above it. Nothing moves, and she needs to see that first.\n2. Rub the same balloon on her hair, twenty strokes, counted out by her.\n3. Hold it back over the tray at the same height. The paper comes up off the metal to meet it.\n4. Rub a second balloon on the wool jumper and run the same test. She calls which one lifted more before either of you looks.\n5. Go hunting with it. Balloon behind her head and her hair follows. Balloon beside a thin stream from the kitchen tap and the water bends over. Balloon near the crisp packet and it slides.\n6. Let her find one more thing in the house that moves. She will try twenty and land one."),
